!96!Interrupt display duration (sec)
!320!How long an interrupted cast stays visible with the interrupt message before the bar hides. 0 hides it immediately.
!96!Max name length
!320!Spell names longer than this many characters are cut and end in '...'. Names are also trimmed to fit the free bar width, so narrow bars may show fewer.
!96!Outline thickness
!320!Width of the border around each castbar, in pixels; 0 removes it. The Interrupt Ready border style colors this border, so keep it above 0 for that style.
!96!Reserved space
!320!Keeps this many extra pixels free next to the spell name, on top of the room kept for the cast time, so long names stay clear of the timer.
!96!Shake on interrupt
!320!Jolts a castbar sideways when the cast it shows is interrupted, so kicks are easy to notice. Applies to every castbar.
!96!Shake strength
!320!How far the bar jolts, in pixels. 0 turns the shake off even while Shake on interrupt is enabled.
!96!Show GCD bar for instant casts
!320!Runs a short castbar for the global cooldown whenever an instant spell triggers it.%0A%0AThe fill and time text are driven natively by the client from the real (haste-scaled) GCD duration - no per-frame addon work while the bar runs. A real cast, channel or empower always takes priority.
!96!Show cast pushback
!320!Appends the delay a cast has accumulated to the spell name, for example "Fireball +0.4".%0A%0AThe delay is read once per cast from the same event that starts the bar.
!96!Show castbar glow effect
!320!Gradually brightens the bar toward white as a cast nears its end, so the last moment of a cast is easy to spot.
!96!Show latency indicator
!320!Shades the end of the Player castbar by your latency or spell queue window, whichever is larger, to help time your next spell. Player castbar only.
!96!Spark extends beyond bar
!320!Lets the spark stick out above and below the bar at about twice its height. Only matters while the spark is shown.
!96!Spell name shortening
!320!Cuts long spell names on every castbar to Max name length and marks the cut with '...'. Reserved space applies only while this is on.
!96!Spell-specific channel tick markers
!320!Shows tick separators on the Player castbar while channeling.%0A%0ASupported spells use their actual tick count, including supported talent and channel-duration changes. Unsupported channels keep five evenly spaced fallback lines. Custom channel tick settings override the automatic layout.%0A%0AThe markers are event-driven and add no recurring channel polling.
!96!Use opposite fill direction for target
!320!Flips the fill direction on the Target castbar only, so it can mirror your Player castbar when the two frames face each other.
